{
  "_comment": [
    "Phase 0: the HTTP-level contract of the Eureka-based Discovery Service, captured from a running",
    "instance (discovery-service, https profile, client-certificate auth) on 2026-09-08.",
    "This is the companion to the body-level fixtures in this directory: those pin what is in a response,",
    "this pins the status code, the selected representation and whether the body is empty.",
    "Two observations that are easy to get wrong and are load-bearing:",
    "  1. XML is the DEFAULT representation. No Accept header, or 'Accept: */*', both yield application/xml.",
    "     Only an explicit 'Accept: application/json' yields JSON. Any client that does not ask specifically",
    "     - which includes most naive HTTP clients and customer curl scripts - is receiving XML today.",
    "  2. A 404 carries a completely empty body and no Content-Type, for reads and writes alike. Returning a",
    "     JSON error document instead breaks enabler reconnect (see api-layer commit 9f58010c6).",
    "Not captured here: /eureka/status and /eureka/lastn. On this configuration /eureka/status returns 500 with",
    "java.lang.NullPointerException 'Cannot invoke String.length() because text is null' from the Freemarker",
    "status view - a pre-existing failure, unrelated to this work, and relevant to decision D4 in",
    "TASK-Discovery-Native-Registry.md: the dashboard being replaced is already not serving here."
  ],
